n\nThen, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}x+{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of sum formula with $a=\\frac{3}{4}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x+\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186507457 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064327 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48f257af-1f00-5cf9-89cd-3d44d21482ec" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Trinomial with Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46bfa4c3-af30-5756-82bb-059f1b23c4a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x-\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506843} {:answer/id #uuid "4850c323-0008-5586-a92c-51d27d9d80e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x-\\frac{25}{6})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506847} {:answer/id #uuid "9af9ba7a-b83f-5100-8ba8-0c8c301f0339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x+\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507013} {:answer/id #uuid "aa4ea64c-142a-5719-b240-6ec5e8ce7a0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x+\\frac{5}{3})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507054} {:answer/id #uuid "b6500cbd-5e5a-59f1-8c25-13b96afe7d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x-\\frac{5}{3})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46bfa4c3-af30-5756-82bb-059f1b23c4a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x-\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506843} :answer-field/id #uuid "f20bb066-c188-50d4-908b-5327e0942d6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8c418bae-22aa-5bc3-86d4-82df570c3162" :question/math-academy-id "q-78927" :question/problem "Factor ${x}^{2}-\\frac{5}{3}x+\\frac{25}{36}.$" :question/worked-solution "The \"square of a difference\" formula states that\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2ax+{a}^{2}=(x-a)^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe will use this formula to factor the given trinomial. Our trinomial is\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-\\frac{5}{3}x+\\frac{25}{36}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-\\frac{5}{3}x+{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{5}{6}x+{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of difference formula with $a=\\frac{5}{6}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x-\\frac{5}{6})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
